/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# NOTE: Cache-Control cannot be set from here. Cloudflare Pages enforces its
# own caching for static assets (public, max-age=14400, must-revalidate) and
# ignores any Cache-Control in _headers — the security headers above do apply,
# so the file itself is working. Consequence: after a deploy, a returning
# visitor's browser may serve a stale .css/.js for up to four hours.
#
# Real fixes, if that becomes a problem:
#   1. Append a version to the asset URLs (/style.css?v=<sha>), ideally
#      injected at deploy time in .github/workflows/deploy.yml.
#   2. A zone-level Cache Rule overriding Browser TTL (needs a token with
#      Zone -> Cache Rules -> Edit; the current CI token does not have it).
